 ### [Tetrahedral Regularization](834-tetrahedral-regularization.md)
-Tetrahedral Regularization is a loss term added to the optimization of tetrahedral mesh vertex positions to prevent elements from becoming inverted (negative volume) or degenerate (volume approaching zero). It solves the problem of mesh validity during differentiable rendering optimization, where high learning rates or discontinuous fields can cause geometric collapse. It sets itself apart from standard surface-only reconstruction methods by explicitly penalizing volumetric degeneracy.
