 ### [Bezier Tetrahedra Evaluation](1422-bezier-tetrahedra-evaluation.md)
-Bezier Tetrahedra (BT) evaluation computes scalar field values within a tetrahedral element using cubic Bernstein polynomials defined by 20 control weights and a bounding tetrahedron. It solves the problem of representing volumetric data on unstructured grids and enables efficient ray-tracing of isosurfaces by reducing intersection to univariate polynomial root finding. It differs from sibling methods like [Adaptive Subdivision in DiffTetVR](807-adaptive-subdivision-in-difftetvr.md), [Tetrahedral Regularization](834-tetrahedral-regularization.md), [DEFTET](6415-deftet.md), and [Initial Skeleton Extraction via Parallel-Plane Sets](11635-initial-skeleton-extraction-via-parallel-plane-sets.md) by using a fixed cubic Bernstein basis on explicit bounding tetrahedra to directly transform ray intersections into screen-space univariate polynomials, rather than relying on adaptive refinement, regularization, or skeleton-based extraction.
