 ### [Initial Skeleton Extraction via Parallel-Plane Sets](11635-initial-skeleton-extraction-via-parallel-plane-sets.md)
-This method extracts the initial geometric skeleton (vertices and edges) of a multi-resolution tetrahedral grid by exploiting its inherent regularity. It represents the grid as a union of parallel-plane sets, where planes sharing the same normal are grouped by their offsets. This approach solves the problem of efficiently identifying the topological structure of unstructured tetrahedral meshes without relying on local neighborhood searches. It sets itself apart from sibling methods like [Adaptive Subdivision in DiffTetVR](807-adaptive-subdivision-in-difftetvr.md) and [DEFTET](6415-deftet.md) by using global linear algebra operations (Kronecker products and matrix inversions) to generate candidate vertices and edges in parallel, rather than iterative refinement or local sampling.
